#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:7
#: de4bc55e7ab14cfd98fcaa3ad1d1fc85
msgid "This article provides advanced configuration information for the :ref:`SiK Telemetry Radio <common-sik-telemetry-radio>`. It is intended for \"power users\", and those who wish to gain a better understanding of how the radios operate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:14
#: 357ded51ce4a4ead957b5f31cabcc3c0
msgid "Most users will only need the basic guide and feature overview provided in :ref:`SiK Radio v2 <common-sik-telemetry-radio>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:21
#: 36ebc54bd0c64e8ea08234ce8cf57c79
msgid "Monitoring the link quality"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:23
#: 202ca332e7e84de4819069b1ad7af124
msgid "You can use the MAVLink support in the SiK Radios to monitor the link quality while flying, if your ground station supports it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:26
#: 9340617410714bf8a559cd7056b76296
msgid "The two key message parameters are ``RADIO.rssi`` and ``RADIO.remrssi``. The first is the RSSI (signal strength) level that the local radio is receiving at. The remrssi parameter is the RSSI that the remote radio is receiving at."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:31
#: 8ccb313cc52442ca9ef36891c474e984
msgid "Here is a typical graph of the RSSI levels for a flight at my local flying field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:37
#: 0d3a476e23c34c0997c99ae05cb1cc65
msgid "The RSSI value scales approximately as 1.9x the dBm signal strength, plus an offset. See the Si1000 data sheet for the exact mapping between RSSI and dBm received signal strength, or use this approximate formula"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:47
#: fc7d7009aed4470c83fad52cfe9db40d
msgid "The reason the RSSI varies so much during this flight is that the signal is attenuated when the plane is rolled over in a turn as I was using a simple wire antenna in the plane. The RSSI values for this flight were plenty high enough for the link quality to be excellent throughout the flight using the default radio parameters."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:56
#: 8f08c78def00411fb1928898c351d2bd
msgid "Diagnosing range problems"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:58
#: e32394bef91b4cd1b3eea3b6e205da88
msgid "If you get less range than you would expect from the above information then what you need to do is graph the noise and signal levels from a flight to work out what the problem is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:62
#: 9ffa071bd7ae46b5b047ed6e60e3f80b
msgid "The most common source of range problems is noise. Noise is unwanted radio emissions in the same frequency range that your radio is using that interferes with the operation of your radio. The radios have telemetry logging built in to help you diagnose the source of the noise."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:67
#: e01b98cb0a4b4f77a50dbf13727cc648
msgid "There are three key types of noise that are likely to affect your radios:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:70
#: 2b402406dc4540c59f21286541cbc89f
msgid "Noise from the electronics in your aircraft (such as your motor, ESC, autopilot etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:72
#: ff5870cd3d0e4f74a43bafe9b6cb803b
msgid "Noise from your ground station computer, especially its USB bus"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-3dr-radio-advanced-configuration-and-technical-information.rst:73
